This crate (`symphonia-codec-qcelp`) is a pure-Rust QCELP 13K (PureVoice) decoder. It is licensed
under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

The decoder is a port of FFmpeg's QCELP decoder (`libavcodec/qcelpdec.c`, `libavcodec/qcelpdata.h`),
which implements TIA/EIA/IS-733 ("High Rate Speech Service Option 17 for Wideband Spread Spectrum
Communication Systems"). The bitmaps, the LSP vector quantization tables, the codebooks and the gain
table (`src/tables.rs`) are extracted programmatically from FFmpeg's `qcelpdata.h`. The LSP to LPC
conversion follows `libavcodec/lsp.c` (`ff_acelp_lspd2lpc`), and the filters follow
`libavcodec/celp_filters.c`, `libavcodec/acelp_filters.c` and `libavcodec/acelp_vectors.c`. These
files are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

